// #465 ACCEPT arm. The three *_rejected.wyn siblings only assert that a bad
// method call fails the build, so "reject every method call on a scalar" would
// satisfy all three. This file is what stops that: a REAL method on each of the
// three receivers the fix touches must still compile, run and print.
//
// One method per receiver, chosen from a different part of each type's dispatch
// table so the file is not just testing `to_string` three times:
//   int   .abs()      -> int_abs
//   float .sqrt()     -> float_sqrt
//   bool  .to_int()   -> bool_to_int
// and one chained call, because a method on a method RESULT is the shape that
// reaches codegen with a receiver the checker never named.
// EXPECT: 42|2|1|7
i = -42
f = 4.0
b = true
print("${i.abs()}|${f.sqrt().to_int()}|${b.to_int()}|${7.max(3)}")
